  Direct messages  4
    One-on-one     3 conversations
    Group          1 conversation
    Messages       243  (80 thread replies, imported as ordinary messages)
    Files          8  (not moved)
    Not migrated   2 conversations

    What happens
    ● These are private conversations. Each is imported into a Teams chat with
      exactly its Slack participants.
    ● A chat is visible to its participants while the import runs, with a notice
      that a migration is in progress.
    ● One-on-one history goes into the chat the two people already have in
      Teams, if they have one.
    ● Files are not moved; each message that had one says so. Thread replies
      become ordinary messages, in time order.
    ● A conversation is imported with all of its participants as themselves, or
      not at all.

    Not migrated
    Conversations   Why
                1   a participant's Slack account is deactivated
                1   a participant has no Microsoft 365 account

  Content  7
    Microsoft Graph cannot import everything Slack stores. This is what Taut
    found and what it will do with each.

    ● 309  Messages with reactions
           Summarized in a line under the message (whether imported reactions
           show in Teams is unconfirmed)

    ! 124  Edited messages
           Final text is imported with an "edited" marker; edit history is not
           available

    ● 102  Bot and app messages
           Attributed to the placeholder account with the bot's name shown

    ● 171  @here / @channel / @everyone
           Converted to plain text so the import notifies nobody

    !  13  Join, leave and topic notices
           Not migrated

    !  80  Thread replies in direct messages
           Imported as ordinary messages, in time order; chats have no threads

    !   8  Files in direct messages
           Not moved; each message says a file was there

    ● transformed   ! information is lost

